1067
01:02:22,430 --> 01:02:30,000
Oh, but... huh?

1068
01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:31,900
No wait, something's off, like one more step...

1069
01:02:31,900 --> 01:02:32,800
Refraction!

1070
01:02:32,800 --> 01:02:34,800
It needs to be refracted

1071
01:02:34,800 --> 01:02:38,600
After catching it directly, what move do I need to make?

1072
01:02:38,600 --> 01:02:40,600
Right, right, right, right

1073
01:02:40,600 --> 01:02:46,220
Like, use the catching momentum to go straight down

1074
01:02:46,220 --> 01:02:50,250
Don't be ridiculous!

1075
01:02:50,250 --> 01:02:56,250
Like, jump in here, use that entry momentum, then spring up from below

1076
01:02:56,250 --> 01:02:58,250
Even the Grand Circus has its limits, that's way too much

1077
01:02:58,250 --> 01:03:04,050
Luna-tan probably just switches it quickly, so the ball just flies on its own

1078
01:03:04,850 --> 01:03:08,650
First catch it, then just let it fly

1079
01:03:08,650 --> 01:03:13,270
The question is where exactly do we do the catch

1080
01:03:13,270 --> 01:03:17,070
Grab this one as it flies by

1081
01:03:17,070 --> 01:03:21,090
The timing is tricky

1082
01:03:21,090 --> 01:03:25,600
Ready, go!

1083
01:03:25,600 --> 01:03:29,690
Which way?

1084
01:03:29,690 --> 01:03:33,090
Oh, I need to be faster

1085
01:03:34,180 --> 01:03:38,180
Move faster. Hmm, this is tough.

1086
01:03:38,180 --> 01:03:39,920
Wait, hold on, that just now.

1087
01:03:39,920 --> 01:03:41,790
I managed to catch it, but...?

1088
01:03:41,790 --> 01:03:44,720
I think Luna-tan needs to move it over here super fast.

1089
01:03:44,720 --> 01:03:45,720
Yeah, you're right.

1090
01:03:45,720 --> 01:03:47,520
From here to here. Wait.

1091
01:03:47,520 --> 01:03:50,320
If we just do that last one faster.

1092
01:03:50,320 --> 01:03:52,320
The circus performer is just running right now.

1093
01:03:52,320 --> 01:03:54,920
So I just need to hit the switch right away.

1094
01:03:54,920 --> 01:04:00,720
Press here, hit the switch, complete the transfer, and that's it.

1095
01:04:00,720 --> 01:04:01,980
That's it

1096
01:04:01,980 --> 01:04:03,040
Got it

1097
01:04:03,040 --> 01:04:05,070
Looks like we can do this

1098
01:04:05,070 --> 01:04:07,640
Let's go for it

1099
01:04:07,640 --> 01:04:11,140
3, 2, 1, go

1100
01:04:11,140 --> 01:04:14,810
Not sure if we'll make it in time

1101
01:04:14,810 --> 01:04:16,210
Sorry, I was a bit too early

1102
01:04:16,210 --> 01:04:17,410
Wait, wait

1103
01:04:17,410 --> 01:04:19,670
Luna-tan was too fast

1104
01:04:19,670 --> 01:04:20,590
The ball...

1105
01:04:20,590 --> 01:04:24,690
Ball transport failed

1106
01:04:24,690 --> 01:04:25,570
It's okay

1107
01:04:25,570 --> 01:04:27,150
Sorry, sorry

1108
01:04:27,150 --> 01:04:29,150
Oh wait, that was actually really good!

1109
01:04:29,150 --> 01:04:34,150
That was great — is there maybe a way to do it mid-air or something?

1110
01:04:34,150 --> 01:04:39,750
Mid-air you probably just catch the ball, right? Boing boing

1111
01:04:39,750 --> 01:04:40,550
Yeah

1112
01:04:40,550 --> 01:04:42,350
Okay, let's try again

1113
01:04:42,350 --> 01:04:44,350
So we really just catch the ball mid-air, huh

1114
01:04:44,350 --> 01:04:48,950
There's no way we have to catch it mid-air AND kill something, right?

1115
01:04:48,950 --> 01:04:49,750
Alright

1116
01:04:49,750 --> 01:04:50,750
Let's go

1117
01:04:50,750 --> 01:04:52,550
Let's try it once after

1118
01:04:52,550 --> 01:04:53,550
Here we go

1119
01:04:53,550 --> 01:04:55,350
3, 2, 1... okay!

1120
01:04:55,350 --> 01:04:58,930
Yes!

1121
01:04:58,930 --> 01:05:00,530
Got it!

1122
01:05:00,530 --> 01:05:01,330
I got it!

1123
01:05:01,330 --> 01:05:04,330
Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah!

1124
01:05:04,330 --> 01:05:10,910
Now! Right now! Wait, does this mean we have to take them down mid-air?!

1125
01:05:10,910 --> 01:05:11,910
Are you serious?!

1126
01:05:11,910 --> 01:05:12,910
No way!

1127
01:05:12,910 --> 01:05:14,910
Hey hey hey hey hey hey!

1128
01:05:14,910 --> 01:05:18,510
But just now, just now, it was looking really good!

1129
01:05:18,510 --> 01:05:22,110
That was SO close just now!

1130
01:05:22,110 --> 01:05:25,110
Wait, so we can't do it in mid-air like that?

1131
01:05:25,110 --> 01:05:28,110
We can't, but that's the only hit point there is.

1132
01:05:28,110 --> 01:05:30,710
Huh?

1133
01:05:30,710 --> 01:05:32,510
Huh?

1134
01:05:32,510 --> 01:05:34,310
Huh?

1135
01:05:34,310 --> 01:05:37,110
Are there two floors?

1136
01:05:37,110 --> 01:05:38,710
Wait, what do you mean?

1137
01:05:38,710 --> 01:05:40,510
That was crazy just now.

1138
01:05:40,510 --> 01:05:44,510
So when we come here, next time we do it this way over here?

1139
01:05:44,510 --> 01:05:52,870
I'll transport them and...

1140
01:05:53,670 --> 01:05:54,670
Huh?

1141
01:05:54,670 --> 01:06:00,470
After transporting like this, the ball bounces like this and jumps—

1142
01:06:00,470 --> 01:06:02,270
Like this?

1143
01:06:02,270 --> 01:06:06,220
Hmm, can we actually do it this way?

1144
01:06:06,220 --> 01:06:12,550
Let's try again.

1145
01:06:12,550 --> 01:06:14,350
So the turret goes there—

1146
01:06:14,350 --> 01:06:18,350
So those 3 and 1 are there for that reason?

1147
01:06:18,350 --> 01:06:20,150
I have no idea.

1148
01:06:20,150 --> 01:06:22,150
Will it loop infinitely?

1149
01:06:22,150 --> 01:06:24,950
Will it become an infinite bounce loop?

1150
01:06:24,950 --> 01:06:31,750
Let's give it a shot. Because those 3 and 1 are right where those guys are, right?

1151
01:06:31,750 --> 01:06:32,750
Yeah, you're right.

1152
01:06:32,750 --> 01:06:34,480
Alright, let's go!

1153
01:06:34,480 --> 01:06:36,350
3, 2, 1, GO!

1154
01:06:36,350 --> 01:06:40,000
Transport complete.

1155
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:40,950
Here we go.

1156
01:06:40,950 --> 01:06:41,950
Flying — okay.

1157
01:06:41,950 --> 01:06:46,470
What just happened? What happened?

1158
01:06:46,470 --> 01:06:47,810
It's flying, it's flying!

1159
01:06:47,810 --> 01:06:49,930
What's happening right now?

1160
01:06:49,930 --> 01:06:51,590
It's in an infinite bounce loop!

1161
01:06:51,590 --> 01:06:53,350
It's in an infinite bounce loop!

1162
01:06:53,350 --> 01:06:55,190
We haven't taken them down.

1163
01:06:55,190 --> 01:06:57,030
Got one!

1164
01:06:57,030 --> 01:06:58,570
Got one!

1165
01:06:58,570 --> 01:07:00,770
That last one over there!

1166
01:07:00,770 --> 01:07:01,550
Nice, nice!

1167
01:07:01,550 --> 01:07:05,050
This turned into an action game!

1168
01:07:05,050 --> 01:07:06,410
We haven't taken them all down yet.

1169
01:07:06,410 --> 01:07:07,710
Still haven't gotten them all.

1170
01:07:07,710 --> 01:07:10,380
Did we get them all?!

1171
01:07:10,380 --> 01:07:20,210
Whoa— wait, huh? Did we get them? Did we? Did we? Did we do it?

1172
01:07:20,210 --> 01:07:30,130
But we can't hear their voices anymore— wait, something's still bouncing— oh nice nice nice, looks like we got them! Oh, they're gone! The right one got obliterated!

1173
01:07:30,130 --> 01:07:37,610
The left one too — I think we did it, I think we're good, we pulled it off! Oh, we might've done it!

1174
01:07:37,610 --> 01:07:46,630
We did it! We did it! We did it! Aaaaaah! This is inhuman — they're actually alive now!

1175
01:07:46,630 --> 01:07:58,630
Woohoo! Oh I see, I see! Really?! So that's how it works?! That's insane! Polka, you're amazing!

1176
01:07:58,630 --> 01:08:14,620
So as a reward, all I have to do is jump? Yeah! Let's go! Woo! Yay! Woo! Yay! Will this work? Won't we get shot? Nope, no getting shot! We're not getting shot!

1177
01:08:14,620 --> 01:08:17,450
Nope, no getting shot!

1178
01:08:17,450 --> 01:08:22,450
We did it! So all Polka has to do is repaint it?

1179
01:08:22,450 --> 01:08:28,170
Yeah, exactly! Alright, let's go — here we go!

1180
01:08:28,170 --> 01:08:32,930
Here we go — let's do this!

1181
01:08:32,930 --> 01:08:37,290
Yay!

1182
01:08:37,290 --> 01:08:42,010
Man, that was tough. There's so much you just can't figure out without trying it.

1183
01:08:42,010 --> 01:08:44,770
Without even thinking, you just move like that?

1184
01:08:44,770 --> 01:08:48,150
The infinite bounce loop appeared again!

1185
01:08:48,150 --> 01:08:56,460
Next up — Dead Seven!

1186
01:08:56,460 --> 01:09:00,360
It looks simple, but the simple ones are always the hardest.

1187
01:09:00,360 --> 01:09:03,820
Right now — so far, it's been hard.

1188
01:09:03,820 --> 01:09:06,160
Nothing has been easy.

1189
01:09:06,160 --> 01:09:10,060
There was not a single easy thing.

1190
01:09:10,820 --> 01:09:12,120
Boing boing boiiing~

1191
01:09:12,120 --> 01:09:15,020
Whoa, whoa!

1192
01:09:15,020 --> 01:09:16,220
Whoa, whoa! Whoa, that's amazing!

1193
01:09:16,220 --> 01:09:18,160
My whole view turned orange!

1194
01:09:18,160 --> 01:09:21,060
There's so much gel!

1195
01:09:21,060 --> 01:09:22,760
The gel is flying everywhere!

1196
01:09:22,760 --> 01:09:24,800
Painting everything is—

1197
01:09:24,800 --> 01:09:26,320
—proper etiquette.

1198
01:09:26,320 --> 01:09:30,000
Oh, so you place the cube here.

1199
01:09:30,000 --> 01:09:32,920
Oh, there's one over here too.

1200
01:09:32,920 --> 01:09:34,020
Got a straight line here!

1201
01:09:34,020 --> 01:09:35,900
Oh, looks like we can jump super high!

1202
01:09:35,900 --> 01:09:37,260
Whoa, amazing!

1203
01:09:37,260 --> 01:09:38,300
Wait, we jump that high?

1204
01:09:38,300 --> 01:09:43,300
Whoooa! We crashed into each other!

1205
01:09:43,300 --> 01:09:45,100
Whoooa!

1206
01:09:45,100 --> 01:09:48,900
I was trying to tackle Polpol. That was scary.

1207
01:09:48,900 --> 01:09:53,700
Whoooa! I'm gonna tackle you!

1208
01:09:53,700 --> 01:09:55,500
Huh? What is this?

1209
01:09:55,500 --> 01:09:58,300
If I do this, the top... wait, what did you do?

1210
01:09:58,300 --> 01:10:02,300
Doesn't it come out from above? The ball comes out from here.

1211
01:10:02,300 --> 01:10:06,100
Oh, the ball comes out from there — wait, it doesn't. It does, it doesn't.

1212
01:10:06,100 --> 01:10:10,970
What is this? The ball isn't getting caught!

1213
01:10:10,970 --> 01:10:12,770
Hmm?

1214
01:10:12,770 --> 01:10:15,570
This thing has no intention of landing on top of it.

1215
01:10:15,570 --> 01:10:20,800
What's with this ball, it just falls...

1216
01:10:20,800 --> 01:10:23,800
Wait, what are we supposed to do about that?

1217
01:10:23,800 --> 01:10:26,600
Is Polpol going to go catch it again?

1218
01:10:26,600 --> 01:10:29,500
But I can't fly or anything.

1219
01:10:29,500 --> 01:10:33,200
I think you use that momentum — jump from here, right?

1220
01:10:33,200 --> 01:10:36,780
I see. Well, I'm used to that much by now.

1221
01:10:36,780 --> 01:10:41,040
But how do we build up speed for this?

1222
01:10:41,040 --> 01:10:44,200
Maybe this?

1223
01:10:44,200 --> 01:10:46,860
This straight line... ah, but hmm, but...

1224
01:10:46,860 --> 01:10:49,860
Can't we go straight into the wall?

1225
01:10:49,860 --> 01:10:51,500
Oh, use the momentum from here?

1226
01:10:51,500 --> 01:10:54,960
Don't tell me it's infinite again? Going along this wall infinitely...

1227
01:10:54,960 --> 01:11:01,520
Oh, that seems likely — the way these are lined up.

1228
01:11:01,520 --> 01:11:08,560
And then like this... infinitely... and then whoosh right here!

1229
01:11:08,560 --> 01:11:16,440
Ahaha! Ahaha! We go, but we also have to activate this side!

1230
01:11:16,440 --> 01:11:21,700
But I get it now. Polka was just daydreaming there.

1231
01:11:21,700 --> 01:11:27,600
Wait, isn't this hard? Okay, so press this here...

1232
01:11:27,600 --> 01:11:30,720
Because Polpol has to stop at some point.

1233
01:11:30,720 --> 01:11:33,480
Oh, she stopped.

1234
01:11:33,480 --> 01:11:34,930
That was a fail.

1235
01:11:34,930 --> 01:11:37,760
One more time, please!

1236
01:11:37,760 --> 01:11:43,520
Oh, no good.

1237
01:11:43,520 --> 01:11:47,380
Tokyo Friend Park!

1238
01:11:47,380 --> 01:11:50,540
This one.

1239
01:11:50,540 --> 01:11:53,640
The ball—

1240
01:11:53,640 --> 01:11:55,120
The ball!

1241
01:11:55,120 --> 01:11:59,920
Please give me the ball!

1242
01:11:59,920 --> 01:12:12,010
So we're supposed to move using this thing here?

1243
01:12:12,010 --> 01:12:14,010
Luna had too much to deal with and came back.

1244
01:12:14,010 --> 01:12:17,010
We have to go back and forth between here and there — I see.

1245
01:12:17,010 --> 01:12:20,010
Polpol is just telling me to run.

1246
01:12:20,010 --> 01:12:24,810
Omaru Polka's debut song—

1247
01:12:24,810 --> 01:12:26,810
Except for Hologram Circus and Po—

1248
01:12:26,810 --> 01:12:28,810
The old-man songs—

1249
01:12:28,810 --> 01:12:30,610
Oh, a little to the side.

1250
01:12:30,610 --> 01:12:32,410
Oh, that didn't work.

1251
01:12:32,410 --> 01:12:33,390
She's listing them all!

1252
01:12:33,390 --> 01:12:38,000
The timing to press it is funny.

1253
01:12:38,000 --> 01:12:39,810
And the footing—

1254
01:12:39,810 --> 01:12:42,610
This is fun!

1255
01:12:42,610 --> 01:12:43,610
Press this one too.

1256
01:12:43,610 --> 01:12:44,610
Magic House!

1257
01:12:44,610 --> 01:12:49,310
And, fire the ball!

1258
01:12:49,310 --> 01:12:50,310
Yes!

1259
01:12:50,310 --> 01:12:52,110
Yes!

1260
01:12:52,110 --> 01:12:52,980
Here we go!

1261
01:12:52,980 --> 01:12:53,910
Come back, please!

1262
01:12:53,910 --> 01:12:54,710
Yes!

1263
01:12:54,710 --> 01:12:57,510
Alright, nice!

1264
01:12:57,510 --> 01:12:59,510
Phew, thank you!

1265
01:12:59,510 --> 01:13:00,510
As expected!

1266
01:13:00,510 --> 01:13:02,310
That was tough, huh.

1267
01:13:02,310 --> 01:13:06,310
Oh, can't we do it with this? This thing.

1268
01:13:06,310 --> 01:13:09,310
Yes!

1269
01:13:09,310 --> 01:13:11,310
Fast, fast!

1270
01:13:11,310 --> 01:13:13,310
Luna-chan, you did great!

1271
01:13:13,310 --> 01:13:19,110
This is less of a puzzle and more just... rage-inducing, right?

1272
01:13:19,110 --> 01:13:21,910
Hurry, hurry!

1273
01:13:21,910 --> 01:13:24,910
Yeah! That was 07!

1274
01:13:24,910 --> 01:13:26,710
Next is 08!

1275
01:13:26,710 --> 01:13:30,710
08, 08 — could that be the weird one?

1276
01:13:30,710 --> 01:13:33,710
The weird one.

1277
01:13:33,710 --> 01:13:35,710
We're using it a lot.

1278
01:13:35,710 --> 01:13:38,710
There's an elevator coming up, and there are turrets too!

1279
01:13:38,710 --> 01:13:40,710
Turrets again?

1280
01:13:40,710 --> 01:13:42,510
Oh yeah, there are turrets.

1281
01:13:42,510 --> 01:14:11,720
Aaaaaaahhh!

1282
01:14:11,720 --> 01:14:13,520
Did you push it and it came out?

1283
01:14:13,520 --> 01:14:15,520
Yeah, I pushed it and it came out

1284
01:14:15,520 --> 01:14:17,320
What came out?

1285
01:14:17,320 --> 01:14:19,320
It's like the ink came out

1286
01:14:19,320 --> 01:14:21,120
What?

1287
01:14:21,120 --> 01:14:22,920
I don't know, nothing's coming out

1288
01:14:22,920 --> 01:14:24,920
Huh? It stopped?

1289
01:14:24,920 --> 01:14:26,720
Just the once?

1290
01:14:26,720 --> 01:14:28,720
It's gushing out over there

1291
01:14:28,720 --> 01:14:30,520
The orange one

1292
01:14:30,520 --> 01:14:32,320
Wait, this light blue one?

1293
01:14:32,320 --> 01:14:34,320
How did that come out?

1294
01:14:34,320 --> 01:14:36,320
Maybe it came out on its own

1295
01:14:36,320 --> 01:14:38,120
Like a cutscene thing

1296
01:14:38,120 --> 01:14:39,090
No idea

1297
01:14:39,090 --> 01:14:39,920
Ah, this...

1298
01:14:39,920 --> 01:14:40,920
Like what...

1299
01:14:40,920 --> 01:14:41,920
What is this thing thinking?

1300
01:14:41,920 --> 01:14:42,720
Heave-ho

1301
01:14:42,720 --> 01:14:43,720
Oh, I made it

1302
01:14:43,720 --> 01:14:45,520
We can get through

1303
01:14:45,520 --> 01:14:47,320
We can get through, but...

1304
01:14:47,320 --> 01:14:48,320
What is this?

1305
01:14:48,320 --> 01:14:50,120
We can get through, but then what?

1306
01:14:50,120 --> 01:14:51,120
Get flow

1307
01:14:51,120 --> 01:14:54,920
Hmm, the ink...

1308
01:14:54,920 --> 01:14:55,920
From over there...

1309
01:14:55,920 --> 01:14:57,720
Like, connect it?

1310
01:14:57,720 --> 01:14:59,720
We can connect it somehow, but...

1311
01:14:59,720 --> 01:15:02,720
Polka can't shoot from this side though

1312
01:15:02,720 --> 01:15:05,520
Like connecting this spot to that one?

1313
01:15:05,520 --> 01:15:07,320
Oh, that I can do

1314
01:15:07,320 --> 01:15:09,120
There! How's that?

1315
01:15:09,120 --> 01:15:12,120
The orange landed over there

1316
01:15:12,120 --> 01:15:16,720
So then Luna connects from there to something else?

1317
01:15:16,720 --> 01:15:18,720
The one behind you, Luna's

1318
01:15:18,720 --> 01:15:20,320
Behind me?

1319
01:15:20,320 --> 01:15:23,120
This one? Yeah, looks like a square

1320
01:15:23,120 --> 01:15:26,020
From here, umm...

1321
01:15:26,020 --> 01:15:29,520
How, how do we do it?

1322
01:15:29,520 --> 01:15:32,510
The ink — how do we connect the ink?

1323
01:15:32,510 --> 01:15:37,380
That window that turned orange — yeah, exactly

1324
01:15:37,380 --> 01:15:42,410
If we connect here... the walking animation is funny

1325
01:15:42,410 --> 01:15:47,530
Splash! Splat! Splosh! Oh, it got overwritten

1326
01:15:47,530 --> 01:15:51,770
The blue one got overwritten — it keeps getting overwritten

1327
01:15:51,770 --> 01:15:55,790
Maybe... whoa, where did it go?

